    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d749">

                <pb facs="0653" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/18462</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Johnson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Brownsville</hi></placeName>, [<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Undated</hi>
                        </date>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">. Received June 17, 1916.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Our cavalry crossed the Rio Grande sixty strong and in less than an hour three
                    hundred more will cross about fourteen miles above <pb facs="0654" n="578"
                        xml:id="pg578"/> Brownsville. By request of General Parker I am staying in
                    Brownsville to-night. More later.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
